"R8-2019-0061 (https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/santaana/board_decisions/adopted_orders/orders/2019/R8-2019-0061.pdf)\nciteturn1148view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 163; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/santaana/board_decisions/adopted_orders/orders/2019/R8-2019-0061.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 6330\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCalifornia Regional Water Quality Control Board (https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/board_decisions/adopted_orders/water_quality/2014/wqo2014_0194_dwq.pdf)\nciteturn1148view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 111; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1143view1\",\"pattern\":\"administratively\"}); Total lines: 4488\nNo matching text found for \"administratively\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCalifornia Regional Water Quality Control Board (https://www.waterboards.ca.gov/board_decisions/adopted_orders/water_quality/2014/wqo2014_0194_dwq.pdf)\nciteturn1148view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 111; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1143view1\",\"pattern\":\"private\"}); Total lines: 4488\nL0@P0: November 18, 2014\nL1@P0: STATE WATER RESOURCES CONTROL BOARD\nL2@P0: 1001 I Street, Sacramento, California 95814\nL3@P0: http://www.waterboards.ca.gov/water_issues/programs/npdes\nL4@P0: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL5@P0: GENERAL ORDER NO. CAG140001\nL6@P0: STATEWIDE NATIONAL POLLUTANT DISCHARGE ELIMINATION SYSTEM\nL7@P0: (NPDES) PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL8@P0: TO WATERS OF THE UNITED STATES\nL9@P0: Discharges from drinking water systems to surface waters in California are subject to waste\nL10@P0: discharge requirements as set forth in this Order, and as authorized by a Notice of Applicability\nL11@P0: issued by the Deputy Director of Water Quality (Deputy Director). Definitions for the purpose\nL12@P0: of this Order are included in Attachment A. Key definitions are as follows:\nL13@P0: Table 1. Key Definitions for the Purpose of this Order\nL14@P0: Drinking\nL15@P0: Water\nL16@P0: System1\nL17@P0: A system with 10002connections or greater that are regulated by the State\nL18@P0: Water Board Division of Drinking Water or a local county department of\nL19@P0: health, with the primary purpose of transmitting, treating and distributing\nL20@P0: safe drinking water. Drinking water systems include state owned/operated\nL21@P0: facilities such as parks, campgrounds, and rest areas\nL22@P0: 1\nL23@P0: This Order applies to community water systems as defined in Attachment A of this Order. This Order\nL24@P0: does not apply to non-community water systems or non-transient water systems as defined in\nL25@P0: Attachment A of this Order.\nL26@P0: 2\nL27@P0: Systems with fewer than 1000 connections that discharge to waters of the United States have the\nL28@P0: option to enroll in this Order. Non-enrollment does not exempt dischargers from Clean Water Act\nL29@P0: requirements.\nL30@P0: Drinking\nL31@P0: Water\nL32@P0: System\nL33@P0: Discharge\nL34@P0: Short-term or seasonal discharges from a drinking water system of water\nL35@P0: that has been dedicated for drinking water purposes\nL36@P0: Water\nL37@P0: Purveyor\nL38@P0: Any entity that discharges from a drinking water system, including water\nL39@P0: purveyors, wholesalers, distributors, districts, municipalities, private\nL40@P0: companies, and other entities that own or operate a community drinking\nL41@P0: water system\nL42@P0: Discharger\nL43@P0: A water purveyor that is authorized to discharge under this Order through an\nL44@P0: approved Notice of Applicability issued by the Deputy Director of Water\nL45@P0: Quality\nL46@P0: Waters of the\nL47@P0: United States\nL48@P0: Generally refers to surface waters, as defined for the purposes of the federal\nL49@P0: Clean Water Act. For the purpose of this Order, the terms “surface water,”\nL50@P0: and “receiving water” are interchangeably used to mean “waters of the\nL51@P0-1: United States,” unless noted otherwiseSTATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEMS DISCHARGES\nL52@P1: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL53@P1: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL54@P1: November 18, 2014 2\nL55@P1: Table 2. Administrative Information\nL56@P1: This Order was adopted by the State Water Board on November 18, 2014:\nL57@P1: This Order shall become effective on February 26, 2015 (100 days after the adoption\nL58@P1: date of this Order)\nL59@P1: This Order shall expire on February 25, 2020\nL60@P1: CERTIFICATION\nL61@P1: I, Jeanine Townsend, Clerk to the Board, do hereby certify that this Order with all attachments\nL62@P1: is a full, true, and correct copy of the Order adopted by the State Water Board on\nL63@P1: November 18, 2014.\nL64@P1: AYE: Chair Felicia Marcus\nL65@P1: Vice Chair Frances Spivy-Weber\nL66@P1: Board Member Tam M. Doduc\nL67@P1: Board Member Steven Moore\nL68@P1: Board Member Dorene D’Adamo\nL69@P1: NAY: None\nL70@P1: ABSENT: None\nL71@P1: ABSTAIN: None\nL72@P1: Jeanine Townsend\nL73@P1-2: Clerk to the BoardSTATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL74@P2: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL75@P2: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL76@P2: November 18, 2014 3\nL77@P2: Table of Contents\nL78@P2: I. Scope of Statewide General Order and Required Regulatory Coverage......................................... 4\nL79@P2: A. Water Purveyors NOT Required to Enroll in This Order ......................................................... 5\nL80@P2: B. Discharges Authorized Under This Order............................................................................... 6\nL81@P2: C. Discharges Not Authorized Under This Order ........................................................................ 7\nL82@P2: II. Permit Coverage and Application Requirements............................................................................. 7\nL83@P2: A. Permit Coverage.................................................................................................................... 7\nL84@P2: B. Permit Effective Date ............................................................................................................. 8\nL85@P2: C. Application Package Requirements ....................................................................................... 8\nL86@P2: D. State Water Board Notice of Applicability............................................................................... 9\nL87@P2: E. Permit Coverage Termination .............................................................................................. 10\nL88@P2: F. Permit Transfer.................................................................................................................... 10\nL89@P2: III. Findings ....................................................................................................................................... 11\nL90@P2: IV. Discharge Specifications and effluent limitations\nL91@P2: (Only Applicable to Discharges that enter a Water of the U.S.)........................................... 13\nL92@P2: V. Receiving Water Limitations ......................................................................................................... 16\nL93@P2: VI. Multiple Uses or Beneficial Reuse ................................................................................................ 16\nL94@P2: VII. Provisions..................................................................................................................................... 17\nL95@P2: A. Standard Provisions............................................................................................................. 17\nL96@P2: B. Monitoring and Reporting Program Requirements ............................................................... 17\nL97@P2: C. Special Provisions................................................................................................................ 17\nL98@P2: D. Noncompliance .................................................................................................................... 17\nL99@P2: VIII. Compliance Determination For Planned Discharges..................................................................... 17\nL100@P2: A. Permit Compliance for Planned Discharges only ................................................................. 18\nL101@P2: B. General................................................................................................................................ 18\nL744@P18: Plan designates beneficial uses, establishes water quality objectives, and contains implementation\nL745@P18: programs and policies to achieve water quality objectives for all waters of the Basin.\nL746@P18: Beneficial Uses\nL747@P18: The existing or potential uses of receiving waters in the permit area as designated by a Regional\nL748@P18: Water Board basin plan or other water quality control plan.\nL749@P18: Best Management Practices (BMPs)\nL750@P18: Methods, measures, or practices designed and selected to reduce or eliminate the discharge of\nL751@P18: pollutants to surface waters from point and nonpoint source discharges. BMPs include structural\nL752@P18: and nonstructural controls, and operation and maintenance procedures, which can be applied\nL753@P18: before, during, and/or after pollution producing activities.\nL754@P18: Community Water System\nL755@P18: A public water system for the provision of water for human consumption through pipes or other\nL756@P18: constructed conveyances that has 15 or more service connections or regularly serves at least 25\nL757@P18: individuals daily at least 60 days out of the year.\nL758@P18: Drinking Water System\nL759@P18: A system regulated by the State Water Resources Control Board Division of Drinking Water or\nL760@P18: a local county department of health, with the primary purpose of conveying, treating, storing\nL761@P18: and distributing safe drinking water to at least 15 service connections used by yearlong\nL762@P18: residents or regularly serves at least 25 year around residents of the area served by the\nL763@P18: system.\nL764@P18: Deputy Director\nL765@P18: The Deputy Director of Water Quality for the State Water Resources Control Board or any\nL766@P18: person(s) delegated by the Deputy Director to serve as acting Deputy Director.\nL767@P18: Direct Discharge\nL768@P18: Any discharge that enters a Water of the U.S. without first traveling via a storm drain or any other\nL769@P18-19: constructed conveyance system.STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL770@P19: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL771@P19: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL772@P19: ATTACHMENT A – DEFINITIONS A-2\nL773@P19: Discharger\nL774@P19: Any water purveyor named in this Order as being responsible for permit requirements within its\nL775@P19: jurisdiction. A discharger to this Order includes a public or private water purveyor, wholesaler, or\nL776@P19: district, or a contractor working on behalf of the water purveyor, wholesaler or district.\nL777@P19: Drinking Water System Discharges\nL778@P19: Release of flows from drinking water intakes, transmission, storage, pumping, treatment and\nL779@P19: distribution systems including flows due to: (1) system failures and pressure releases, (2) system\nL780@P19: development, testing and maintenance that is performed to comply with the federal Safe Drinking\nL781@P19: Water Act, the California Health and Safety Code, and State Water Board Division of Drinking\nL782@P19: Water permit requirements.\nL783@P19: Emergency Discharge\nL784@P19: A discharge due to a sudden unexpected occurrence involving a clear and imminent danger,\nL785@P19: demanding immediate action to prevent or mitigate loss of, or damage to, life, health, property, or\nL786@P19: essential public services, including the provision of drinking water supplies in accordance with\nL787@P19: applicable drinking water statutes and regulations.\nL788@P19: Estuaries\nL789@P19: Surface waters, including coastal lagoons, located at the mouths of streams that serve as\nL790@P19: areas of mixing for fresh and ocean waters. Estuarine waters shall be considered to extend\nL791@P19: from a bay or the open ocean to a point upstream where there is no significant mixing of fresh\nL792@P19: water and seawater.\nL793@P19: Enclosed Bays\nL794@P19: Enclosed bays are hydrological indentations along the coast that enclose an area of oceanic\nL795@P19: water within distinct headlands or harbor works. Enclosed bays include all bays where the\nL796@P19: narrowest distance between the headlands or outermost harbor works is less than 75 percent\nL797@P19: of the greatest dimension of the enclosed portion of the bay.\nL798@P19: Impaired Water Body\nL799@P19: A water body that is currently listed on the Clean Water Act section 303(d) list.\nL800@P19: Indirect Discharge\nL801@P19: Any discharge that enters a Water of the U.S. by first traveling via a storm drain or any other\nL802@P19: constructed conveyance system.\nL803@P19: Inland Surface Waters\nL804@P19: All surface waters of the state that do not include the ocean, enclosed bays, or estuaries.\nL805@P19: Low Impact Development (LID)\nL806@P19: A storm water management and land development strategy that emphasizes water\nL807@P19: conservation and the use of on-site natural features integrated with engineered, small-scale\nL808@P19-20: hydrologic controls to more closely reflect pre-development hydrologic functions.STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL809@P20: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL810@P20: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL811@P20: ATTACHMENT A – DEFINITIONS A-3\nL812@P20: Method Detection Limit (MDL)\nL813@P20: Minimum concentration of a substance that can be measured and reported with 99 percent\nL814@P20: confidence that the analyte concentration is greater than zero, as defined in in 40 C.F.R. part\nL815@P20: 136, Attachment B, revised as of July 3, 1999.\nL816@P20: Minimum Level (ML) and Reporting Level (RL)\nL817@P20: The minimum level (ML) means the concentration at which a properly calibrated monitoring\nL818@P20: system gives a recognizable signal and acceptable calibration point. The ML is the\nL819@P20: concentration in a sample that is equivalent to the concentration of the lowest calibration\nL820@P20: standard analyzed by a specific monitoring procedure, assuming that all the method specified\nL821@P20: sample weights, volumes, and processing steps have been followed. A reporting level (RL) is\nL822@P20: the ML for reporting and compliance determination included in this Order.\nL823@P20: MS4 Operator\nL824@P20: The MS4 Operator is the entity responsible for the operation of its local municipal separate\nL825@P20: storm sewer system subject to an MS4 NPDES Permit.\nL826@P20: Monitoring Well\nL827@P20: Specialized wells in which the depth to groundwater can be measured and samples of ground\nL828@P20: water can be collected for analysis for the purpose of managing drinking water aquifers and/or\nL829@P20: to fulfill requirements mandated by the federal Safe Drinking Water Act and the California\nL830@P20: Health and Safety Code.\nL831@P20: Non-community Water System\nL832@P20: A water system that is not a community water system, as defined in this attachment. A non\u0002community water system is a water system that generally serves less than 15 service\nL833@P20: connections used by yearlong residents or does not regularly serve at least 25 year around\nL834@P20: residents with the water system’s service area.\nL835@P20: Not Detected (ND)\nL836@P20: Sample results less than the properly calibrated monitoring equipment’s MDL.\nL837@P20: Non-transient Water System\nL838@P20: A water system that is not a community water system, as defined in this attachment, and that\nL839@P20: regularly serves at least 25 of the same persons over six months per year. Non-transient\nL840@P20: water systems are regulated by the State Water Board Division of Drinking Water.\nL841@P20: National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System (NPDES)\nL842@P20: The national program for issuing, modifying, revoking and reissuing, terminating, monitoring\nL843@P20: and enforcing permits, and imposing and enforcing pretreatment requirements, under Clean\nL844@P20: Water Act sections 307, 402, 318, and 405.\nL845@P20: Pollutants\nL846@P20: Substances defined in Clean Water Act section 502(6) (33 U.S.C. § 1362(6)), and incorporated\nL847@P20-21: by reference into Water Code section 13373.STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL848@P21: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL849@P21: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL850@P21: ATTACHMENT A – DEFINITIONS A-4\nL851@P21: Pollution Prevention\nL852@P21: Any action that causes a net reduction in the use or generation of a hazardous substance or\nL853@P21: other pollutant that is discharged into water and includes, but is not limited to, input change,\nL854@P21: operational improvement, production process change, and product reformulation (as defined in\nL855@P21: Water Code section 13263.3). Pollution prevention does not include actions that merely shift a\nL856@P21: pollutant in discharge water from one environmental medium to another environmental\nL857@P21: medium, unless clear environmental benefits of such an approach are identified to the\nL858@P21: satisfaction of the State Water Board or Regional Water Board.\nL859@P21: Receiving Water\nL860@P21: The term receiving water is used interchangeably with the term waters of the U.S.\nL861@P21: Superchlorinated Water\nL862@P21: Water that is dosed with chlorine in order to adequately sanitize and disinfect drinking water\nL863@P21: system facilities\nL864@P21: Supply Well\nL865@P21: A groundwater well that is installed, operated, maintained and/or rehabilitated in accordance\nL866@P21: with the federal Safe Drinking Water Act and the California Health and Safety Code to pump\nL867@P21: ground water for the primary purpose of delivering drinking water to a municipality or\nL868@P21: community.\nL869@P21: Transmission Systems\nL870@P21: Transmission systems include pipes, pumps, canals, pump houses, and other components\nL871@P21: used to move water from the point of origin to storage reservoirs, treatment facilities, and\nL872@P21: distribution systems. Transmission systems do not have connections to serve end users.\nL873@P21: Water Purveyor\nL874@P21: Any entity that discharges from a drinking water system, including water purveyors,\nL875@P21: wholesalers, distributors, districts, municipalities, private companies, and other entities that\nL876@P21: own or operate a community drinking water system.\nL877@P21: Water Wholesaler\nL878@P21: An entity that provides potable water to a person, political subdivision, or municipality that is\nL879@P21: not the ultimate consumer of the service.\nL880@P21: Waters of the State\nL881@P21: Any surface water or groundwater, including saline waters, within boundaries of the state.\nL882@P21: Waters of the United States (U.S.)\nL883@P21-22: Generally refers to surface waters, as defined for the purposes of the federal Clean Water Act.STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL884@P22: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL885@P22: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL886@P22: ATTACHMENT B1 and B2 – NOTICE OF INTENT and NOTICE OF NON-APPLICABILITY B-1\nL887@P22: B.\nL888@P22: ATTACHMENT B1 – NOTICE OF INTENT\nL889@P22: STATE WATER RESOURCES CONTROL BOARD\nL890@P22: TO APPLY FOR REGULATORY COVERAGE UNDER\nL891@P22: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ, NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL892@P22: FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES TO WATERS OF THE U.S.\nL893@P22: 1. DRINKING WATER SYSTEM OWNER1\nL894@P22: Name Number of Connections:__________________\nL895@P22: State Water Board Division of Drinking Water Drinking Water System No.:_______________\nL896@P22: (If Applicable - Conceptual Letter Approval – System No.:___________________________)\nL897@P22: Mailing Address\nL898@P22: City State ZIP Phone\nL899@P22: Contact Person\nL900@P22: Signature:2 Date:\nL901@P22: 2. APPLICANT (IF DIFFERENT FROM SYSTEM OWNER)\nL902@P22: Name\nL903@P22: Mailing Address\nL904@P22: City State ZIP Phone\nL905@P22: Contact Person\nL906@P22: Signature:2 Date:\nL907@P22: 3. WATER SUPPLIERS (IF APPLICABLE)\nL908@P22: Name\nL909@P22: Mailing Address\nL910@P22: City State ZIP Phone\nL911@P22: Contact Person\nL912@P22: Signature:2 Date:\nL913@P22: 4. BILLING ADDRESS\nL914@P22: Name\nL915@P22: Mailing Address\nL916@P22: City State ZIP Phone\nL917@P22: Contact Person\nL918@P22: \nL919@P22: 1\nL920@P22: If additional property owners are involved, provide the information in a supplementary letter.\nL921@P22: 2\nL922@P22: By signing this notice of intent, you are certifying under penalty of perjury that the information provided in this\nL923@P22: application and in any attachments is true and accurate to the best of your knowledge. By signing this Notice of\nL924@P22: Intent, you agree to closely monitor and stop the discharge if there is any violation of Order WQ 2014-0194-\nL925@P22-23: DWQ or impact to receiving water beneficial uses. STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL926@P23: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL927@P23: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL928@P23: ATTACHMENT B1 and B2 – NOTICE OF INTENT and NOTICE OF NON-APPLICABILITY B-2\nL929@P23: 5. PLANNED DISCHARGE INFORMATION\nL930@P23: Identify the type of facilities that will have drinking water system discharge (all that apply)\nL931@P23: Intake and/or Transmission Facilities Distribution Systems\nL932@P23: Storage Tanks and/or Reservoirs Supply Wells\nL933@P23: Water Treatment Facilities Other (explain below)\nL934@P23: List and description of other discharges.\nL935@P23: Are the discharges existing discharges as of the adoption date of this Order)? ___________\nL936@P23: If not, identify the new discharges that are proposed to take place prior to the expiration date of this Order?\nL937@P23: List any additives to the drinking water not affiliated with drinking water treatment, their purpose, and quantity:\nL938@P23: (For example, algaecides, anticorrosion agents, etc.)\nL939@P23: 6. MULTIPLE WATER USE OR BENEFICIAL USE OPTIONS\nL940@P23: Is using a portion of the discharge for irrigation, groundwater infiltration/recharge\nL941@P23: or other use a viable option?\nL942@P23: Yes No\nL943@P23: Is land disposal of a portion of your discharge a viable option? Yes No\nL944@P23: Provide a brief description of the discharge (or portion thereof), that is collected and applied for irrigation or other\nL945@P23: beneficial reuse. If no multiple water use options of any portion of your discharge are viable, explain why (attach\nL946@P23-24: additional sheet as necessary). STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL947@P24: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL948@P24: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL949@P24: ATTACHMENT B1 and B2 – NOTICE OF INTENT and NOTICE OF NON-APPLICABILITY B-3\nL950@P24: 7. RECEIVING WATER INFORMATION (provide on separate sheet if necessary) Note that\nL951@P24: identification of receiving waters does not necessarily constitute a formal finding that any specific water\nL952@P24: body is a water of the U.S.\nL953@P24: Name of all named receiving water bodies and/or major downstream water bodies:\nL954@P24: Circle the Regional Water Quality Control Board(s) where receiving water body (ies) is/are located:\nL955@P24: REGION 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, or 9\nL956@P24: (See Attachment H for identification of the various regions)\nL1167@P32: ATTACHMENT D – STANDARD PROVISIONS D-1\nL1168@P32: D.\nL1169@P32: ATTACHMENT D – STANDARD PROVISIONS\nL1170@P32: I. STANDARD PROVISIONS – PERMIT COMPLIANCE\nL1171@P32: A. Duty to Comply\nL1172@P32: 1. The Discharger shall comply with all of the conditions of this Order. Any\nL1173@P32: noncompliance constitutes a violation of the Clean Water Act (CWA) and the\nL1174@P32: California Water Code (Water Code) and is grounds for a potential enforcement\nL1175@P32: action, permit termination, revocation and reissuance, or modification; or denial of a\nL1176@P32: permit renewal application. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(a).)\nL1177@P32: B. Need to Halt or Reduce Activity Not a Defense\nL1178@P32: It shall not be a defense for a permittee in an enforcement action that it would have\nL1179@P32: been necessary to halt or reduce the permitted activity in order to maintain compliance\nL1180@P32: with the conditions of this Order. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(c).)\nL1181@P32: C. Duty to Mitigate\nL1182@P32: The Discharger shall take all reasonable steps to minimize or prevent any discharge in\nL1183@P32: violation of this Order that has a reasonable likelihood of adversely affecting human\nL1184@P32: health or the environment. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(d).)\nL1185@P32: D. Proper Operation and Maintenance\nL1186@P32: The Discharger shall at all times properly operate and maintain all facilities and systems\nL1187@P32: of treatment and control (and related appurtenances) which are installed or used by the\nL1188@P32: Water Purveyor to achieve compliance with the conditions of this Order. Proper\nL1189@P32: operation and maintenance also includes adequate laboratory controls and appropriate\nL1190@P32: quality assurance procedures. This provision includes the operation of backup or\nL1191@P32: auxiliary facilities or similar systems that are installed by a Water Purveyor only when\nL1192@P32: necessary to achieve compliance with the conditions of this Order. (40 C.F.R. §\nL1193@P32: 122.41(e).)\nL1194@P32: E. Property Rights\nL1195@P32: 1. This Order does not convey any property rights of any sort or any exclusive\nL1196@P32: privileges. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(g).)\nL1197@P32: 2. The issuance of this Order does not authorize any injury to persons or property or\nL1198@P32: invasion of other private rights, or any infringement of state or local law or\nL1199@P32: regulations. (40 C.F.R. § 122.5(c).)\nL1200@P32: F. Inspection and Entry\nL1201@P32: The Water Purveyor shall allow State and/or Regional Water Board staff, United States\nL1202@P32-33: Environmental Protection Agency (U.S. EPA), and/or their authorized representatives STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL1203@P33: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL1204@P33: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL1205@P33: ATTACHMENT D – STANDARD PROVISIONS D-2\nL1206@P33: (including an authorized contractor acting as their representative), upon the\nL1207@P33: presentation of credentials and other documents, as may be required by law, to\nL1208@P33: (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(i); Water Code section 13383):\nL1209@P33: 1. Enter upon the Discharger’s premises where a regulated facility or activity is located\nL1210@P33: or conducted, or where records are kept under the conditions of this Order\nL1211@P33: (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(i)(1));\nL1212@P33: 2. Have access to and copy, at reasonable times, any records that must be kept under\nL1213@P33: the conditions of this Order (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(i)(2));\nL1214@P33: 3. Inspect and photograph, at reasonable times, any facilities, equipment (including\nL1215@P33: monitoring and control equipment), practices, or operations regulated or required\nL1216@P33: under this Order (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(i)(3)); and\nL1217@P33: 4. Sample or monitor, at reasonable times, for the purposes of assuring Order\nL1218@P33: compliance or as otherwise authorized by the CWA or the Water Code, any\nL1219@P33: substances or parameters at any location. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(i)(4).)\nL1220@P33: II. STANDARD PROVISIONS – PERMIT ACTION\nL1221@P33: A. General\nL1222@P33: This Order may be modified, revoked and reissued, or terminated for cause. The filing\nL1223@P33: of a request by the Discharger for modification, revocation and reissuance, or\nL1224@P33: termination, or a notification of planned changes or anticipated noncompliance does not\nL1225@P33: stay any Order condition. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(f).)\nL1226@P33: B. Duty to Reapply\nL1227@P33: If the Discharger chooses to continue a discharge regulated by this Order after the\nL1228@P33: expiration date of this Order and after the State Water Board has reissued this Order,\nL1229@P33: the Discharger shall apply for and obtain new permit coverage as required by the new\nL1230@P33: Order. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(b).)\nL1231@P33: C. Transfers\nL1232@P33: This Order is not transferable to any person except after notice to the State Water\nL1233@P33: Board. The State Water Board may require modification or revocation and reissuance\nL1234@P33: of the Order or Notice of Applicability to change the name of the Discharger and\nL1235@P33: incorporate such other requirements as may be necessary under the CWA and the\nL1236@P33-34: Water Code. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(l)(3) and 122.61.)STATEWIDE GENERAL NPDES PERMIT FOR DRINKING WATER SYSTEM DISCHARGES\nL1237@P34: ORDER WQ 2014-0194-DWQ\nL1238@P34: NPDES NO. CAG140001\nL1239@P34: ATTACHMENT D – STANDARD PROVISIONS D-3\nL1240@P34: III. STANDARD PROVISIONS – MONITORING\nL1241@P34: A. Samples and measurements taken for the purpose of monitoring shall be representative\nL1242@P34: of the monitored activity. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(j)(1).)\nL1243@P34: B. If applicable, monitoring results shall be conducted according to test procedures under\nL1244@P34: 40 Code of Federal Regulations part 136. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(j)(4) and 122.44(i)(1)(iv).)\nL1245@P34: IV. STANDARD PROVISIONS – RECORDS\nL1246@P34: A. Records Retention\nL1247@P34: The Discharger shall retain records of all monitoring information, including all calibration\nL1248@P34: and maintenance records and all original strip chart recordings for continuous\nL1249@P34: monitoring instrumentation, copies of all reports required by this Order, and records of\nL1250@P34: all data used to complete the application for this Order, for a period of at least three (3)\nL1251@P34: years from the date of the sample, measurement, report or application. This period may\nL1252@P34: be extended by request of the State Water Board’s Division of Water Quality Deputy\nL1253@P34: Director at any time. (40 C.F.R. § 122.41(j)(2).)\nL1254@P34: B. Records of monitoring information shall include:\n"
